   "title": "Russian Discount Retailer Fix Price Exits Mongolia",
   "url": "https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2026/11/02/russian-discount-retailer-fix-price-exits-mongolia-a94155",
   "domain": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "source": "themoscowtimes.com",
   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:48:03 +0300",
   "_dt": 1793630883.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "The discount retail chain Fix Price has completely pulled out of Mongolia, with all three of its stores in the East Asian country having shut down by the end of September, the newspaper Vedomosti reported Monday, citing the company’s third-quarter 2026 financial results. Industry analysts told Vedomosti that Mongolia’s small market size and logistical challenges in the country likely made it difficult for Fix Price to run a sustainable business there.",
   "summary_zh": "折扣零售连锁企业 Fix Price 已彻底撤出蒙古。该东亚国家的3家门店均已于9月底前关闭。《Vedomosti》周一提报道称，公司引用了其2026年第三季度的财务业绩。行业分析师向《Vedomosti》表示，蒙古市场规模较小，运营物流面临困难，这些因素可能使 Fix Price 难以在当地维持可持续经营。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The discount retail chain Fix Price has completely pulled out of Mongolia, with all three of its stores in the East Asian country having shut down by the end of September, the newspaper Vedomosti reported Monday, citing the company’s third-quarter 2026 financial results. Fix Price did not publicly comment on the reasons behind the market exit. Industry analysts told Vedomosti that Mongolia’s small market size and logistical challenges in the country likely made it difficult for Fix Price to run a sustainable business there. Fix Price first entered Mongolia in January 2023, when it opened two franchise locations in the capital, Ulaanbaatar. Inventory for those stores was delivered by truck from a distribution center in Novosibirsk across the border. The chain briefly expanded to four locations by late 2025 before scaling back. Besides its exit from Mongolia, Fix Price reduced its franchises in Kyrgyzstan from six to four stores and in the United Arab Emirates from four to three. In contrast, Fix Price locations in Uzbekistan grew from 25 to 30, and it opened 10 new stores in Serbia over the three-month reporting period. Founded in 2007, Fix Price is Russia’s largest value retailer with 8,219 stores across 10 countries. Belarus and Kazakhstan are its primary foreign markets with 411 and 408 stores, respectively. In 2023, Fix Price moved its corporate jurisdiction from Cyprus to Kazakhstan after its 2021 initial public offering on the London Stock Exchange. We are facing unprecedented challenges. Russia's Prosecutor General's Office has designated The Moscow Times as an \"undesirable\" organization, criminalizing our work and putting our staff at risk of prosecution. This follows our earlier unjust labeling as a \"foreign agent.\" These actions are direct attempts to silence independent journalism in Russia. The authorities claim our work \"discredits the decisions of the Russian leadership.\" We see things differently: we strive to provide accurate, unbiased reporting on Russia. We, the journalists of The Moscow Times, refuse to be silenced. But to continue our work, we need your help . Your support, no matter how small, makes a world of difference. If you can, please support us monthly starting from just $ 2. It's quick to set up, and every contribution makes a significant impact. By supporting The Moscow Times, you're defending open, independent journalism in the face of repression. Thank you for standing with us",
