   "title": "Troops destroy kidnappers’ hideout in Kogi, recover ammunition",
   "url": "https://www.vanguardngr.com/2026/11/troops-destroy-kidnappers-hideout-in-kogi-recover-ammunition/",
   "domain": "vanguardngr.com",
   "source": "vanguardngr.com",
   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 14:45:52 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793630752.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Troops of the Nigerian Army have destroyed a suspected kidnappers’ hideout in Edimogbo Forest, Igalamela/Odolu Local Government Area of Kogi State, recovering 1,000 rounds of ammunition, six motorcycles and other items. The operation was carried out by troops of the 21 Battalion Quick Reaction Force following intelligence reports indicating the presence of suspected kidnappers in the forest.",
   "summary_zh": "尼日利亚陆军部队摧毁了科吉州伊加拉梅拉/奥杜洛地方政府辖区埃迪莫格博森林一处疑似绑架者藏匿点，并缴获1,000发弹药、6辆摩托车及其他物品。根据情报显示疑似绑架者藏身于该森林，第21营快速反应部队随后采取了此次行动。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Troops of the Nigerian Army have destroyed a suspected kidnappers’ hideout in Edimogbo Forest, Igalamela/Odolu Local Government Area of Kogi State, recovering 1,000 rounds of ammunition, six motorcycles and other items. The operation was carried out by troops of the 21 Battalion Quick Reaction Force following intelligence reports indicating the presence of suspected kidnappers in the forest. The Acting Director of Army Public Relations, Col. Appolonia Anele, disclosed this in a statement on Monday. She said the troops mobilised to locate the suspected criminals after receiving credible human intelligence about their activities. “On approaching the hideout, the suspected kidnappers, on sighting the advancing troops, fired a shot to alert other members of the group before fleeing deeper into the forest. “The troops immediately pursued the fleeing criminals deep into the forest, but no contact was made,” she said. Anele said the troops subsequently destroyed the camp, including its supporting structures. Items recovered from the hideout included 1,000 rounds of 7.62mm by 54 ammunition, seven bandoliers, two shovels, a hand pump, a mobile phone, a Glo modem, two packets of soap and a jerrycan of Premium Motor Spirit (PMS). Other items recovered were clothing, pairs of shoes and six daylong motorcycles. She said troops were still combing the surrounding area in a bid to track down the fleeing suspects. The Army, according to her, remains committed to sustaining offensive operations against kidnappers and other criminal elements threatening the safety and security of law-abiding citizens. It also urged members of the public to continue providing credible and timely information to security agencies to support efforts to dismantle criminal networks. Comments expressed here do not reflect the opinions of Vanguard newspapers or any employee thereof",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
