   "title": "Korean envoy to US vows support for bilateral investment at Hyundai's Alabama plant",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/business/companies/20261031/korean-envoy-to-us-vows-support-for-bilateral-investment-at-hyundais-alabama-plant",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:27:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793456823.0,
   "ageDays": 2.04,
   "summary": "WASHINGTON — Korean Ambassador to the United States Kang Kyung-wha has pledged to strengthen cooperation with U.S. authorities to support bilateral investment, describing Hyundai Motor Group's latest investment in Alabama as an example of the expanding economic partnership between the two countries. Kang made the remarks Wednesday while attending a ceremony announcing Hyundai Motor Manufacturing Alabama's plan to invest about $450 million in its Montgomery plant, according to the Korean Embassy in Washington.",
   "summary_zh": "华盛顿——韩国驻美国大使姜京华承诺加强与美国当局的合作，以支持双边投资，并将现代汽车集团最新对阿拉巴马州的投资视为两国经济伙伴关系不断扩大的例证。据韩国驻华盛顿大使馆介绍，姜京华周三出席了一场宣布现代汽车制造阿拉巴马州公司计划向其蒙哥马利工厂投资约4.5亿美元的仪式，并发表上述讲话。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "WASHINGTON — Korean Ambassador to the United States Kang Kyung-wha has pledged to strengthen cooperation with U.S. authorities to support bilateral investment, describing Hyundai Motor Group's latest investment in Alabama as an example of the expanding economic partnership between the two countries. Kang made the remarks Wednesday while attending a ceremony announcing Hyundai Motor Manufacturing Alabama's plan to invest about $450 million in its Montgomery plant, according to the Korean Embassy in Washington. The ambassador highlighted Hyundai's presence in the U.S. as an \"outstanding example\" of how the Korea-U.S. alliance has evolved over more than seven decades, expanding beyond its security foundations into cooperation in economic security and advanced technology. Kang also said the investment would combine Korea's advanced manufacturing capabilities with America's innovation and market competitiveness, allowing the two countries to \"shape the future of the automotive industry together,\" according to the embassy. She added that the Korean government would work closely with U.S. federal, state and local governments to continue supporting \"mutually beneficial investments and economic cooperation.\"",
