   "title": "Mahama must apologise to Akufo-Addo over honorary doctorates",
   "url": "https://www.myjoyonline.com/mahama-must-apologise-to-akufo-addo-over-honorary-doctorates-nana-akomea/",
   "domain": "myjoyonline.com",
   "source": "MyJoyOnline（加纳）",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:58:54 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793455134.0,
   "ageDays": 2.06,
   "summary": "The Third National Vice Chairman of the New Patriotic Party (NPP), Nana Akomea, has asked President John Dramani Mahama to apologise to former President Nana Akufo-Addo for his past comments criticising the conferment of honorary degrees on serving presidents. In a Facebook post on Thursday, Mr Akomea recalled that when Mr Akufo-Addo received honorary awards during his presidency, Mr Mahama questioned the appropriateness of such recognition while a person was still in office.",
   "summary_zh": "新爱国党（NPP）第三届全国副主席纳纳·阿科梅亚敦促加纳总统约翰·德拉马尼·马哈马，就过去批评向在任总统授予荣誉学位的言论向前总统纳纳·阿库福-阿多道歉。阿科梅亚先生周四在Facebook上发帖称，阿库福-阿多先生任内获得荣誉奖项时，马哈马先生曾质疑一个人在任期间接受此类表彰是否恰当。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Third National Vice Chairman of the New Patriotic Party (NPP), Nana Akomea, has asked President John Dramani Mahama to apologise to former President Nana Akufo-Addo for his past comments criticising the conferment of honorary degrees on serving presidents. Mr Akomea says the President’s acceptance of another honorary doctorate from a university in Russia exposes what he considers an inconsistency in the position Mr Mahama previously held on the matter. In a Facebook post on Thursday, Mr Akomea recalled that when Mr Akufo-Addo received honorary awards during his presidency, Mr Mahama questioned the appropriateness of such recognition while a person was still in office. He said the then-opposition leader had argued that Mr Akufo-Addo should have waited until after his presidency to allow for a proper assessment of his record before receiving honorary doctorates. Mr Akomea also recalled Mr Mahama’s suggestion that the former president was using the influence of his office to secure such honours from universities. However, Mr Akomea noted that President Mahama, who has been in office for less than two years, had himself received three or four honorary doctorates, including the latest recognition in Russia. Expressing mixed feelings about the latest award, he said he was happy for President Mahama but considered his acceptance of the honour inconsistent with the criticism he had directed at his predecessor. “For the sake of his Integrity, President Mahama owes President Akufo-Addo an unqualified apology on this matter of honorary awards,” he wrote",
