   "title": "COPEC projects petrol price to fall; diesel to go up on November 1 pricing window",
   "url": "https://www.myjoyonline.com/copec-projects-petrol-price-to-fall-diesel-to-go-up-on-november-1-pricing-window/",
   "domain": "myjoyonline.com",
   "source": "MyJoyOnline（加纳）",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:12:49 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793445169.0,
   "ageDays": 2.17,
   "summary": "The Chamber of Petroleum Consumers (COPEC) is predicting petrol prices to go down while diesel price go up at the pumps in the first pricing window starting, November 1, 2026. In statement, COPEC forecast petrol price to go down by 1.71 and diesel to go up by 4.07 percent. According to COPEC, Free On Board price of petrol decreased from $1255.05 per Metric Tonne to $1199.16 per Metric Tonne indicating a -4.45%.",
   "summary_zh": "石油消费者委员会（COPEC）预计，在从2026年11月1日开始的第一个定价窗口内，各加油站的汽油价格将下降，而柴油价格将上涨。COPEC在一份声明中预测，汽油价格将下降1.71%，柴油价格将上涨4.07%。据COPEC称，汽油离岸价格从每公吨1255.05美元降至每公吨1199.16美元，降幅为4.45%。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Chamber of Petroleum Consumers (COPEC) is predicting petrol prices to go down while diesel price go up at the pumps in the first pricing window starting, November 1, 2026. In statement, COPEC forecast petrol price to go down by 1.71 and diesel to go up by 4.07 percent. According to COPEC, Free On Board price of petrol decreased from $1255.05 per Metric Tonne to $1199.16 per Metric Tonne indicating a -4.45%. “With a currency appreciation of about 0.6%, the retail price of petrol works up to Ghc16.72 per litre representing 1.71% decrease of the current mean price of Ghc17.02 per litre Thus, the retail price of Petrol is expected to be selling between GHS15.89 per litre and GHS17.57 per litre, within a ±5% range of COPEC's projection”. On diesel, COPEC said the Free On Board price of the product increased marginally from 1414.78 per Metric Tonne to $1453.07 indicating a 2.71%. “The cedi’s appreciation of 0.6%, the projected retail pump price for diesel in the next window shall work up to Ghc19.15 per litre representing a 4.07% increase of the current mean rice of Ghc18.40 per litre. Thus, diesel is expected to sell within a range of Ghc18.19 per litre minimum to Ghc20.11 per litre maximum within a ±5% range of COPEC's projection”",
