   "title": "Russia Africa Summit: 22 Presidents The Russia Africa Summit 2026 closed in Moscow with 48 countries and 22 heads of state, up from 17 in 20",
   "url": "https://x.com/chomcho/status/2116329551345115430",
   "snippet": "Russia Africa Summit: 22 Presidents\n\nThe Russia Africa Summit 2026 closed in Moscow with 48 countries and 22 heads of state, up from 17 in 2023. \n\nPutin promised no \"neo-colonial exploitation\" and declared the era of a few states deciding \"the fate of entire continents\" over.\n\nWhat he wanted: Africa's 54 UN votes, military reach through the Africa Corps, minerals, and a trade system beyond sanctions. Grain is Russia's main tool of influence: 13 million tonnes of farm products in the first nine months of 2026. \n\nThe political return appeared in February 2026, when six African states voted against a UN peace resolution on Ukraine and 17 abstained.\n\nWhat Africa wanted: weapons, cheap grain, power plants, a bigger UN voice, and the freedom to deal with everyone. Mali's leader, General Assimi Goïta, asked for \"partnerships based on sovereignty, equality and non-interference.\"\n\nTrade figures show that Russia is a much smaller partner. \n\nTrade with Africa in 2025: Europe 385,000 million dollars, China 348,000 million dollars, the United States about 85,000 million dollars, Russia 27,000 million dollars. \n\nThe United States total is less than half its trade with Vietnam alone. Russia's real weight is the Africa Corps, about 2,000 men in the Sahel.\n\nNo leader mentioned the African recruits: 3,066 Africans lured into Russia's army with job offers, 502 confirmed dead. Two days before the summit, a UN commission called it trafficking.\n\nIn the Sahel, the Africa Corps saved Niger's junta from a mutiny but cannot lift the jihadist fuel blockade on Bamako, the capital of Mali. Egypt, an ally of the United States, is building a 25,000 million dollar nuclear plant with Russia.\n\nThe answer of the United States government is \"commercial diplomacy\" and minerals deals. This is the right approach, but the Russian government brought together 22 presidents, and the United States has not.\n\nTrade beats mercenaries. The United States must be present in Africa, or other countries will take its place.\n\nRead the full story here:\nhttps://t.co/LKcMK0is9t\n\nRelated Links:\nThe Africa Corps in Mali and the Civilians Nobody Is Protecting — https://t.co/8FqZWPg9FH\nRussia Sudan Alliance: Weapons, Gold, and a Naval Base on the Red Sea — https://t.co/X8U6bNrIIX\nAfrica Integration Crisis Deepens as America and China Compete —",
   "body": "Russia Africa Summit: 22 Presidents\n\nThe Russia Africa Summit 2026 closed in Moscow with 48 countries and 22 heads of state, up from 17 in 2023. \n\nPutin promised no \"neo-colonial exploitation\" and declared the era of a few states deciding \"the fate of entire continents\" over.\n\nWhat he wanted: Africa's 54 UN votes, military reach through the Africa Corps, minerals, and a trade system beyond sanctions. Grain is Russia's main tool of influence: 13 million tonnes of farm products in the first nine months of 2026. \n\nThe political return appeared in February 2026, when six African states voted against a UN peace resolution on Ukraine and 17 abstained.\n\nWhat Africa wanted: weapons, cheap grain, power plants, a bigger UN voice, and the freedom to deal with everyone. Mali's leader, General Assimi Goïta, asked for \"partnerships based on sovereignty, equality and non-interference.\"\n\nTrade figures show that Russia is a much smaller partner. \n\nTrade with Africa in 2025: Europe 385,000 million dollars, China 348,000 million dollars, the United States about 85,000 million dollars, Russia 27,000 million dollars. \n\nThe United States total is less than half its trade with Vietnam alone. Russia's real weight is the Africa Corps, about 2,000 men in the Sahel.\n\nNo leader mentioned the African recruits: 3,066 Africans lured into Russia's army with job offers, 502 confirmed dead. Two days before the summit, a UN commission called it trafficking.\n\nIn the Sahel, the Africa Corps saved Niger's junta from a mutiny but cannot lift the jihadist fuel blockade on Bamako, the capital of Mali. Egypt, an ally of the United States, is building a 25,000 million dollar nuclear plant with Russia.\n\nThe answer of the United States government is \"commercial diplomacy\" and minerals deals. This is the right approach, but the Russian government brought together 22 presidents, and the United States has not.\n\nTrade beats mercenaries. The United States must be present in Africa, or other countries will take its place.\n\nRead the full story here:\nhttps://t.co/LKcMK0is9t\n\nRelated Links:\nThe Africa Corps in Mali and the Civilians Nobody Is Protecting — https://t.co/8FqZWPg9FH\nRussia Sudan Alliance: Weapons, Gold, and a Naval Base on the Red Sea — https://t.co/X8U6bNrIIX\nAfrica Integration Crisis Deepens as America and China Compete —",
